WEBVTT

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.360
The Sinner!

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.610
The Sinner has come!

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.490
Aion!

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.450
Aion has come!

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.800
You certainly gave me a hard time.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.760
It doesn't matter, because in
the end, you'll be destroyed by Aion!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.430
There's no place for you humans to run!

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.350
Aion...

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.690
The darkness has been growing
more turbulent ever since that day.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:17.780
What is Aion?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.910
So you finally found him?

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.290
It's been so long.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:30.120
The papers themselves
were in their hands at one point,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.880
so we can't be entirely sure about this,

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.590
but it looks like we can
uncover his tracks with these.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:38.090
Speaking of which, where is Rosette?

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.720
She went to the place
where all of this began.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.100
At Seventh Bell?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.720
I see...

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.150
Wow...

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:58.110
This place would draw too many eyes
if we had left it as it was. That's why.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.120
Wait up, please!

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.050
Where was the switch?

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.670
I have a feeling that it was this way.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.050
Well... Wait, you two!

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.980
Rosette?

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.620
Rosette, where are you?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:53.250
Please answer me...

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.550
Rosette? Are you over there?

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.440
Oh, it's just a board.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.940
A board?

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.240
Azmaria!

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.800
Oww...

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.970
Are you all right, Azmaria?

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:44.880
It hurts.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.640
That's because you screamed
all of a sudden when you saw my face.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.890
But...

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.100
It was four years ago.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.230
Winter, four years ago.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:02.190
This place is still just
like that time, that night.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.700
It will remain
unchanged from here on as well.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.360
A world where everything is frozen.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.580
Joshua did this?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.540
It wasn't Joshua!

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.040
It was Aion!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.000
Aion did this!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.170
Azmaria, if you've decided to fight,

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:23.380
then it would be wise for you to
take a good look at what Aion has done.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.840
At what he was trying to start.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.640
Hey! Wait!

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.360
Oh, you guys! Cut it out already!

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.690
Moron! That's against the rules!

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.900
Rosette's serious!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.530
This is bad, she's going to kill us!

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.820
What are you going
to do about the laundry?!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.240
If you're going to play around,
then play around over there!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.290
Hey! Wait!

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.250
Rosette, that's enough!

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.420
Rosette, go for it!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.210
Why, you...

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.050
You're not getting away!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.090
Ow ow ow...

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.850
Billy, you're going to be
taking responsibility for this!

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:15.680
Responsibility?

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:16.930
That's right!

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.650
You're going to wash
the things that you got dirty!

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.190
Yay!

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:26.070
But it's your turn today, Rosette!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:30.360
After what just happened,
you're still saying that?

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.120
Hey, what happened to the bucket?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.080
It's over there.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.920
Joshua, Joshua, hold on!

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.590
Joshua, Joshua!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.130
Should I go get the teacher?

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:48.590
Oh, Joshua!

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.560
I got you! I got you!

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:01.060
There's no way a wild throw
like that would hit anything!

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.690
Oh, that was fun!

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.980
Why, you...

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:15.620
Are you all right, Joshua?
Did you take your medicine?

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.950
Yeah.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:23.130
I feel good today,
so let me stay outside a little more.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.340
Joshua...

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.090
Please, Rosette.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.380
Okay.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:36.060
Rosette, isn't the Minister
coming this afternoon?

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.060
Then why don't we be daring
and go even further outside?

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.310
Rosette!

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.360
Joshua again?

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.400
Well, it can't be helped.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.860
After all, if we're not careful
around him, Miss Jean gets annoying!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.330
Then today, as well...

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:59.370
Yes, when I had taken
my eyes off of her for just a moment...

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.750
I'm sorry.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.000
It can't be helped.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.800
And you say that you wish to take Joshua?

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.260
Yes, he possesses a special talent.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:16.800
Because of that, we would most
certainly like to bring him into our Order.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.640
We have been searching for quite some time

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:22.060
for people who have
the same special abilities as he does.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:26.400
I was thinking that it would
be nice if I could actually meet him.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:29.570
I think that it is a very good offer.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.860
But more than Joshua himself, Rosette is...

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.200
It does seem that his sister really hates me.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.750
Those siblings really do get along well.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:47.040
She probably believes that
her younger brother will be taken away.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.090
Hey, Rosette, how far are we going to go?

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.510
Is it all right for us to stay
out like this and not go back?

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:58.050
It's all right! We're not going
back until the Minister gives up!

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.600
In the first place, he's strange!

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.730
If you trust someone like that,
what do you think will happen?!

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.900
You might get put into
a strange experimental device,

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.440
get experimented on mercilessly,

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.940
and end up pickled in formalin!

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.490
Rosette, you read too many strange books.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.280
Really? I got all of that
out of your dime novels.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:23.620
But he came here from New York, right?

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.000
It might be more fun than
being out in the countryside here.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.880
It's a convent! It's not like
you'd be living in the city.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.630
But when we turn fifteen,
we have to leave here anyway,

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.970
so I don't think that there's
any difference in going there now.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.510
I don't want to.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:43.970
Your body is weak, so it would be
dangerous to leave you by yourself.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.100
You're being a busybody.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.770
Oh, but that's my duty as your older sister.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.970
I can't breathe...

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.550
I'm sorry, Rosette.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.680
Owww!

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.850
The water is...

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.190
Where is this?

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:32.980
Oww...

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.240
Rosette! Are you all right?

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.910
I'm not all right, it cut me to the bone!

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:41.410
You just scraped your knee, is all.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.280
But it hurts!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.910
You're hopeless.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.140
Thank you.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:06.060
This is all I have that's
deserving of thanks, right, Rosette?

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:10.390
Don't say such
foolish things. Let's find the exit.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:11.400
Why...

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:17.570
Why can't I heal my
own injuries or sicknesses?

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.860
If I could...

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.370
It's all right!

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.790
You use your power for other people,

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.870
and I'll protect you, no matter what!

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.580
Now, let's go.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:42.510
What a huge door. It's got to be the exit!

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.260
There's something written here.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:54.730
"An eternal... becoming...
saint... Magda... sleeping?"

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:55.940
Do you understand it?

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.730
It's no use. It's worn away, so I can't read...

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:11.750
It opened.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:12.790
Yeah.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.580
Is this really the exit?

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:17.590
Now that I think about it,

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:20.170
Miss Jean said something about this before.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:23.680
That deep in the forest was someone's grave.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:24.800
A grave?!

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:35.270
It's a coffin.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.150
Then this place really is...

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.150
Who?

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:52.910
Who is the one that has awakened me?

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.620
Well, who are you?

00:12:55.620 --> 00:13:00.550
I'm Chrono.
I'm what you people call a devil.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:04.260
What do you mean by devil?

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:11.470
Just what I said.
A thing that you humans fear.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.730
Hey, are you all right?

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.770
It looks like I don't
have enough spiritual energy.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:22.360
I don't really understand,
but do you mean that you're hungry?

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.320
Wait just a second.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.200
Here you are, eat up!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.750
T-Thank you.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.460
And that's how I met Chrono.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.250
At first, I thought,

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:41.630
"Who is this guy, calling himself a devil?"

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:42.880
That's mean!

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.630
You guys were pretty strange yourselves.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:52.720
But you know, becoming
friends with a devil was cool, right?

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.430
Especially for Joshua,
since he liked the occult.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.890
Right.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:59.230
But I wonder why?

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.770
When I first met Chrono,

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:04.570
I was so afraid I couldn't help myself,

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:06.740
but it went away, like it had never been.

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:10.910
Well...

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.370
Whose coffin was it?

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.370
The holy woman, Magdalene.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:22.040
It's a name that makes
us Sinners feel very uneasy.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:24.500
Why were you at that person's grave?

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:30.840
I'm sorry, I didn't
mean it like that at all.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:34.770
That is...well...

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.440
Chrono!

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.530
Over here!

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:58.870
Yesterday, they finally
said we could go outside.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.330
It's funny!

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.210
Even though he was sick in bed, he didn't
talk about anything but your stories, Chrono.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:06.840
But Chrono's stories are really interesting.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.880
Even you looked like
you were going to cry during

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:11.470
"The Wind Master"
and "The Thunderbird's Story."

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:13.300
Well, those will make you cry.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.760
If that story didn't make you cry,

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.680
it just goes to show
your personality's too twisted.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.890
I don't want to hear
that from <i>you</i>, Rosette.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.890
What do you mean by that?

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.900
A great river that flows in the Heavens?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.780
A great river in the heavens...
Do you mean the Milky Way?

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:32.990
No, I'm talking about
the invisible Astral Line.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.120
Astral Line?

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.870
Right, it flows very far away,

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:41.410
and is made up of the source of all life.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.750
You might be able to
call it fragments of life force.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:52.300
Those fragments fall
to the Earth, combine with a life,

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.100
become a soul, and are born.

00:15:55.100 --> 00:16:00.140
And a soul whose life has
ended goes back into the Heavens,

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:04.230
returns to being a fragment,
and goes back into the great river.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:11.530
They say that this giant cycle has been
continuing on this planet for billions of years.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:15.780
Then, if we go there,
we can meet people who have died?

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:17.200
I wonder?

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:20.500
Actually, I'm just repeating
what I heard someone else say.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:31.170
Incredible!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:34.340
That's incredible, Chrono! It's the
first time I've heard something like that!

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:37.100
Most people don't realize it,

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:41.180
but it's certain that people's
souls continue to flow in this world.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.310
All right! This settles it!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:44.480
Settles what?

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.610
Actually, it's our dream to become explorers.

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:52.820
Africa, the Amazon, the Antarctic,

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:56.200
the two of us will go to
places no one else has ever been.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:59.410
And we're going to
write our records in books!

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:03.200
And if we can find the Astral Line too,
then that would be a great discovery!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.920
And he was so excited.

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.720
I think he got tired because
he was running around too much.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:18.010
But thank goodness.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:21.850
He hasn't been talking
about his dreams lately,

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:24.600
so I thought that he
might have given up on them.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.650
Since he started
being able to use his power,

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:29.730
he's been prone to getting sick,
and his fits have gotten worse.

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:35.030
It's strange, isn't it?

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:38.530
Joshua can't heal his
own injuries or sicknesses.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:46.750
Chrono, I'd rather
become a doctor than an explorer.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.330
For Joshua's sake?

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:49.290
Yeah.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.710
You're so kind.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:56.090
But I wonder if it's impossible.
There's no way for me to become one.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.260
God is pretty unfair, isn't he?

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:02.600
Chrono, keep this
a secret from Joshua, okay?

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:03.520
Okay.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.230
Thank you.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:12.690
Just a little more! Go for it, Chrono!

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:15.400
You did it!

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.950
Rosette!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:29.920
Chrono!

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:24.850
What's wrong, Rosette?

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.430
He...

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:28.890
Joshua decided by himself!

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:34.730
There are some minor formalities,
so I'll come again tomorrow.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.110
You'll be leaving in one week.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.400
Until then, it would be best
to take it easy and recuperate.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:41.490
Yes, Sir.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.580
We won't know until
we do a full examination,

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:48.540
but it looks like the power is
putting a strain on your body.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.580
But why, all of a sudden?

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.920
She's strong.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:06.600
Always energetic and running around,
shouting out at the top of her loud voice.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.390
But she's gentle, just to me.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.650
She's the kind of
person who never holds back,

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:16.230
but it's been so tough for me.

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:20.240
That's why I don't
want her worrying so much.

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:24.030
Minister...

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:28.910
If I go, will I be able to become strong?

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:34.580
Rosette...

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:42.880
What's wrong?

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:44.300
Chrono!

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:45.800
Stay back!

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:48.470
You mustn't come any closer, Rosette!

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.100
Yo, Chrono.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:55.440
Long time no see. Have you been well?

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:58.770
Aion!

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:03.900
Let's do it together again, Chrono.
